{
 "ideas": [
  {
   "id": 12,
   "name": "Rising Goo",
   "approach": "handmade",
   "approachWhy": "Each variant is a tower shape plus a goo speed, and fairness depends on the exact climb time, so hand-made towers with tested speeds are safer than random ones. The clean shapes (stairs, shaft, spiral, ladders, basin) are few, so a generator would add little.",
   "engine": {
    "have": [
     "rising sections with a step path the tests check (gap at most 6, rise at most 3.5 per step)",
     "slide motion on axis y: a big red slab on slide y already gives the Tide Pool tide",
     "slide motion on axis z (Sliding Ledges)",
     "climbable truss ladders (shape \"truss\")",
     "sectionAt and the fall rule: dropping below the lowest platform sends you back to start"
    ],
    "new": [
     {
      "what": "\"flood\" motion: a red see-through slab filling the lane that starts rising when the local player steps onto the section (or passes a start arch), at a set speed or a speed curve (start speed, end speed, like idea 24's 'collapse' wave), with optional pause heights, a stop height, surges and a wave; it drains when you leave or reset",
      "size": "M"
     },
     {
      "what": "hazard touch = back to the start pad (the shared rule from idea 1, used by every hazard idea), plus a server goo check: the server knows when the runner entered the section, works out the goo height itself and sends them back if they are under it",
      "size": "M"
     },
     {
      "what": "\"float\" option on a platform: it rides on top of the flood surface (height = goo height + 0.5), bobbing a little, for Float Up",
      "size": "S"
     },
     {
      "what": "drain valve: reuse the key pickup from idea 20 (touch hides it, chime, client counter); here a touch pauses the flood for a few seconds",
      "size": "S"
     },
     {
      "what": "looks and sound: bubbling goo surface, height marks on the tower wall, a glowing high-water line, rim glow + tick before a surge (tick from idea 18's client beat clock), bubbling that gets louder as it nears you",
      "size": "S"
     },
     {
      "what": "test: walk the step path at walk speed with a slow 1.5 s per jump and check the goo never reaches the player's feet (same shape as idea 24's runner test)",
      "size": "S"
     }
    ]
   },
   "readability": "The goo is the same red see-through hazard as everywhere else, bubbling and filling the bottom of a tower; height marks on the wall and bubbling that gets louder as it nears you show how much time you have. Pauses show as a glowing ring on the rest ledge; surges show as the rim glowing and ticking first.",
